1
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:07,500
You may wonder:

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,041
if surgery physically removes the cancer
from the body,

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:16,083
and systemic therapies also go throughout
the body to target the cancer cells,

4
00:00:16,291 --> 00:00:18,916
Why is radiation necessary?

5
00:00:18,916 --> 00:00:22,000
Radiation plays an important role
either alone

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,708
or in partnership
with these other treatment methods.

7
00:00:26,208 --> 00:00:28,916
Surgery and Radiation Therapy

8
00:00:28,916 --> 00:00:30,916
Some tumors are localized to one

9
00:00:30,916 --> 00:00:35,541
area of the body, and surgery
can be effective in removing the tumor.

10
00:00:35,541 --> 00:00:39,625
However, surgeons are only able
to take out the bulk of the tumor

11
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:44,791
that they can see or that is safe
to remove without harming other organs.

12
00:00:44,791 --> 00:00:48,208
As a result,
there may be cells left over in the body

13
00:00:48,208 --> 00:00:52,833
that the surgeons could not see
and thus could not completely remove.

14
00:00:53,041 --> 00:00:56,250
Radiation to the surgical bed
after surgery,

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:59,833
helps to target any remaining cells
so that those leftover

16
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:03,916
cancer cells
do not continue to grow and divide.

17
00:01:04,083 --> 00:01:07,083
One analogy that may be helpful is this:

18
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,666
surgery is like physically pulling weeds
out of your garden,

19
00:01:10,666 --> 00:01:14,500
and radiation is like spraying weedkiller
in the patches of soil

20
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,333
after to prevent
the growth of further weeds.

21
00:01:19,916 --> 00:01:22,916
Systemic Treatments and Radiation Therapy

22
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,333
With systemic treatments,

23
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:28,541
radiation can work 
 synergistically with these agents

24
00:01:28,541 --> 00:01:32,791
to make the chemo or immunotherapy
even more powerful.

25
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:37,583
This is dependent on the type of cancer
you have and its molecular markers,

26
00:01:37,583 --> 00:01:42,125
and the exact recipe of treatment
may vary from person to person,

27
00:01:42,125 --> 00:01:45,083
tailored to your specific situation.

28
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:50,000
Your radiation oncologist and medical
oncologist will work together to determine

29
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,708
if and when both agents are appropriate
for you.

30
00:01:53,916 --> 00:01:58,166
Some individuals get chemotherapy
before they have radiation.

31
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:03,208
Some individuals get chemotherapy
 at the same time as radiation

32
00:02:03,208 --> 00:02:04,875
And others get chemotherapy

33
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:08,333
after finishing the course of radiation.

34
00:02:08,541 --> 00:02:10,666
Often in head and neck cancers,

35
00:02:10,666 --> 00:02:14,333
chemotherapy can be used to enhance
the effect of radiation.

36
00:02:14,875 --> 00:02:18,541
What we call
radiosensitizing chemotherapy.
